Feature: The equality of the two shapes, checked when the second of a pair is recorded
  A suite of the bench's own, beside the living features: it makes the graph lose a claim between
  the graph arm's run and the prose arm's, which no living scenario can, to see the bench refuse
  to give the prose arm content the graph arm was not given (contracts/arm.md).

  Scenario: a run whose shape does not hold the pair's content is failed
    Given a frozen cohort "november" with a prospective question "rates"
    And the question "rates" has an evidence pack of "4" documents
    And the appraisal of "rates" is made
    And the graph loses a claim once the arm "graph" has been given it
    When the arms "graph" and "prose" forecast "rates"
    Then the run of the arm "prose" is recorded as failed, saying the two shapes did not hold the same content
